== a grid is a set of sets ==
  rows:        3
  columns:     3
  square[1][2] is 6
  the whole of it:
    1 2 3
    4 5 6
    7 8 9
== a cube is a set of grids ==
  layers:         2
  cube[1][0][1] is 6
  the whole of it:
    layer 0:
      1 2
      3 4
    layer 1:
      5 6
      7 8
== every row is its own set ==
  row lengths: 1 2 3 
  a row kept and grown: 3 long now
  a row added:          4 rows now
== transposing ==
  before:
    1 2 3
    4 5 6
  after :
    1 4
    2 5
    3 6
  twice :
    1 2 3
    4 5 6
== multiplying ==
  a          :
    1 2
    3 4
  b          :
    5 6
    7 8
  a times b  :
    19 22
    43 50
  b times a  :
    23 34
    31 46
  a times one:
    1 2
    3 4
== turning a point ==
  start        :  3 1
  after turn 1 :  -1 3
  after turn 2 :  -3 -1
  after turn 3 :  1 -3
  after turn 4 :  3 1
== turning in space ==
  start       :  1 2 3
  turned once :  -2 1 3
  turned twice:  -1 -2 3
  combined    :  -1 -2 3
== turning the cube ==
  before:
    layer 0:
      1 2
      3 4
    layer 1:
      5 6
      7 8
  turned:
    layer 0:
      3 1
      4 2
    layer 1:
      7 5
      8 6
